{"id": "wwdc2019-228", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/228", "wordCount": 4400, "segments": [{"start": 14.0, "text": "Good morning, and thank you"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "for coming to our session."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "At Apple, we build technologies."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "We build technologies so that"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "you can make great apps with"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "amazing experiences."}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "And my favorite apps are the"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "ones that seamlessly blend those"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "technologies and really immerse"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "us in the experience."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "Today we'd like to talk to you"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "about two of these technologies:"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "Core ML and ARKit."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "Both of these help our devices"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "gain a level of understanding"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "about the world around us."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "They help us blend the physical"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "and virtual worlds."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "Today we're going to take you on"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "a journey of building an app"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "that does just that."}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "Along the way, we're going to"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "look at some challenges that we"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "faced and how we overcame them,"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "and we're going to look at some"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "themes that arose from facing"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "those challenges."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "The first, being the question,"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "can machine learning help?"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "Well, okay, if I said no, then"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "this would be a pretty short session."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "But I can't just say a blanket"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "yes, because the answer really"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "depends on the type of problem"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "you're trying to solve and the"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "data you have to solve it,"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "because machine learning is"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "about understanding data."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "It's about understanding"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "patterns in data, patterns in"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "data that may be difficult to"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "write down programmatically."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "And this data exists in your"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "apps."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "Your users enter it every day."}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "They use the keyboard and they"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "enter text."}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "They use the microphone and they"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "record sound."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "They use the camera and they"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "capture video and pictures."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "So when facing a problem, asking"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "yourself, can machine learning"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "help, is a good question to ask."}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "Now, you need to take a close"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "look at the problem you're"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "trying to solve and the data you"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "have available to solve it."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "The second theme that we're"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "going to look at today is"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "understanding the behavior of"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "your model."}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "These models are trained to"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "expect certain inputs in certain"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "formats and to provide outputs"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "in certain formats."}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "And so if your input is not in"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "the format that's expected for"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "the model, then the output is"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "going to be unexpected as well."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "And speaking of outputs, if you"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "don't understand what's being"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "output from your model, it's"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "going to be difficult to use it"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "to make that magical experience"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "in your app."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "We're going to look at a couple"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "ways that you can visualize the"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "inputs and the outputs of some"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "models."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "But for now, on with our"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "journey."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "We said that we're going to"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "combine technologies to blend"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "the physical and virtual worlds,"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "and what better context to do"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "this in than an app?"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "We thought that it would be fun"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "to build an educational game app"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "for children to practice their"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "math skills, like counting, or"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "addition, or multiplication."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "And we know that children"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "sometimes use dice to practice"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "these skills."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "Now, we could've just put"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "virtual dice in the app and let"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "those roll around on the screen,"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "but we thought, wouldn't it be a"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "lot more fun if the children"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "could play with physical dice"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "and roll those on the table and"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "then interact with our app?"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "So that's what we did."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "And the first challenge that we"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "ran into was, how do you get an"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "app to recognize dice?"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "Well, there's a couple"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "approaches."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Let's start programmatically."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "But this is going to be a little"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "difficult."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "If we constrain our problem to"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "only six-sided dice, we can"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "start to look at the properties"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "of a die."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "For instance, the die behind me,"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "its color is gray."}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "But not all dice are gray, so"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "that's not necessarily helpful."}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "If you look at it in a 2D plane,"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "it's a hexagon shape and it has"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "three skewed squares for sides."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "But those move and change as the"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "die rolls around on the table."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "If we take a closer look at each"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "side, there's a number of dots"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "on them; but again, that's"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "different depending on the side"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "you're looking at and depending"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "on your perspective of the die."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "So with all of these properties"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "changing, it's going to be"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "pretty difficult to write a"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "program to recognize dice."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "So let's take a look at the"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "machine learning approach."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "We could train an image"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "classification model to"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "recognize dice in an image."}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "But we want to know how many"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "dice are in an image -- not just"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "the existence of dice in an"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "So instead, we looked at using"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "an object detection model."}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "An object detection model will"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "tell us if there's dice in an"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "image, but it will also tell us"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "where it is in the image; and if"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "we know where the dice are in"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "the image, then we can count"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "them. To do this, we needed to get"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "data, so we took a bunch of"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "pictures of dice rolling around"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "on the table."}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "Next, we took those pictures and"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "we annotated them with bounding"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "boxes, indicating where the dice"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "are in the images."}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "After that, we used the new"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "Create ML to train our custom"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "object detection model."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "If you'd like to learn more"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "about this training, please see"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "the Create ML for Object"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "Detection and Sound Classification session."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "Now I'd like to invite Scott up"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "to show you this in action."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "Scott?"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "Good morning, everyone."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Morning!"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "As Brent discussed, we're"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "going to be exploring adding the"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "ability for our app to count"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "dice using a machine learning"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "technique called object"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "detection."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "And I'm sure you're all eager to"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "see it in action, so let's get"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "right to it."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "So here, we have a very simple"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "app that's wired with a live"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "camera view, and we've added our"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "object detector trained to"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "detect dice so that we can count"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "So let's see what happens when"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "we add dice to the frame."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "One, two, three, and four."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "We can even take a roll for more"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "fun."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "So this is great."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "Our app is able to count dice"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "using object detection."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "But one of the themes that we"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "want to discuss with you today"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "is understanding your model's"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "behavior."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "So let's actually take a look at"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "a debug visualization of what"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "the model is seeing."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "As you can see, we're drawing"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "bounding boxes around each of"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "the detected objects -- in this"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "case, dice -- on the board."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "And if we move them around,"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "those boxes will move as well."}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "This is important to you because"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "if you are training an object"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "detector and you start playing"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "around with it, and you don't"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "notice certain boxes around"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "objects that aren't what you're"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "trying to detect, or you're not"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "seeing boxes around the objects"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "that you are trying to detect,"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "this is probably the opportunity"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "for you to go and collect more"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "data in this kind of lighting."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "You may want to collect more"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "data with different kinds of"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "backgrounds, different lighting,"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "with a different number of"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "objects -- in this case, we have"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "four, but you may want to"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "collect with five, six, up to"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "ten dice, or less, or even"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "images without them to train it"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "to not recognize other objects."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some code"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "to do this."}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "When you use your object"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "detector that you've trained"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "with Create ML, in the Vision"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "framework, what you get back as"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "a result is a list of VN"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "recognized object observations."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "So here we have a function that"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "handles those observations and"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "does a couple things for us."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "The first one is the easiest:"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "we're just counting dice."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "And this just is as simple as"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "counting the number of observations because we have one"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "per die."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "Next, we have a couple helper"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "functions that help us draw"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "these bounding boxes on screen"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "based on these recognized object"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "observations."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "We have a first function that"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "matched the bounds you get from"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "each recognized object"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "observation, which come in"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "normalized coordinates based on"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "the input image you provide to"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "Vision, so that function maps"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "those back to our view"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "controller's views coordinate"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "system so that we can"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "appropriately draw them on"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "screen, overlaying them on top"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "of the actual objects."}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "Next we have a helper function"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "that creates our beautiful"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "rounded rectangles that we"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "display on screen, which is a"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "CALayer, and we add that CALayer"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "to an overlay layer to be"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "rendered on screen."}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "All this code is available in"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "the sample app associated with"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "this session, which I encourage"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "you to check out."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "So this is really promising: our"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "app is able to count dice using"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "object detection."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "But you may have already"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "realized or thought about the"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "fact that games typically don't"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "rely on the count of dice; they"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "typically rely on the values"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "displayed on them."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "So we need to take this one step"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "further and figure out how to"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "recognize the values displayed"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "on these dice."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "This is ultimately the goal that"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "we want our app to have: we want"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "it to be able to tell that the"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "die on the right side is a 5 and"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "the one on the left is a 1."}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "Luckily for us, as Brent"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "mentioned, object detectors can"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "not only detect but classify"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "objects, because they're built"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "to be able to recognize all"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "sorts of different objects and"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "So we went ahead and updated all"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "our training data to actually"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "consider dice with different"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "values to be of a different"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "class, just like you can see on"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "the screen."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "So this sounded really"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "promising, and so we gave it a"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "try in our app."}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some of the"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "examples that we ran into."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "In most cases, it worked"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "perfectly fine."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "As you can see in the picture"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "behind me, our object detector"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "is able to correctly and"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "accurately detect and classify"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "the dice on the left of the"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "screen; but if we focus in on"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "the other side, we can see that"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "our object detector is actually"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "detecting the 6 and the 4 as one"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "single die."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "And if we think a little bit"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "about what's happening, it's"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "clear that the model isn't able"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "to tell those apart as two"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "separate dice, and it really"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "comes down to the fact that the"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "4 is being occluded by the one"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "in front."}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "So after thinking about this a"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "little bit, what we realized was"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "that we really care about the"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "tops of these dice, and those"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "are always visible in our frame."}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "So we went ahead and we helped"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "our model a little bit."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "We updated all our training data"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "to actually focus in on the tops"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "of these dice."}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "So now we're actually training"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "an object detector, not to"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "detect dice, but to detect tops"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "of dice."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "So let's take a look at what"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "happened when we did that."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "As you can see, our model was"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "still able to correctly predict"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "and classify the same dice as"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "before, but now it's also able"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "to correctly detect and identify"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "the dice on the right."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "We wanted to share with you"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "another anecdote today."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "At some point along our journey,"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "we noticed this behavior, where"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "our model was actually detecting"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "the left side of the dice,"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "consistently."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "This was very confusing at"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "first, but if we actually rotate"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "this image, we can understand"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "how the model thought these were"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "the tops."}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "This was super easy to realize"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "as soon as we looked at the input of our model."}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "We were simply not handling the"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "image orientation according to"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "our device's orientation, which"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "is a very common problem for"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "Vision tasks."}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "So the key lesson here is, if"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "you notice odd behavior in your"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "model's output, it doesn't hurt"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "to take a look at the input."}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "It may be as simple as rotating"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "your image based on the"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "orientation of the device."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "So let's see this new model in"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "action."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "So here we have the same app,"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "but we updated it to have our"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "model that's able to detect and"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "classify diced as well."}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "For simplicity, I'm going to"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "focus on three dice."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "We can see that our model is"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "predicting 6, 5 and 2."}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "So let's take a roll."}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "Four, 6 and 5."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "Awesome. This is really"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "promising."}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "So I want to bring your"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "attention to a detail here that"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "I think is very important."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "If I move the dice around, you"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "can see that the list updates."}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "We're actually displaying the"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "list of values according to the"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "order in which the dice are laid"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "out on the table."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "This is a minor design detail,"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "but it really brings consistency"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "to the experience, because the"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "user is seeing these dice laid"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "out in that fashion on the"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "table."}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "So since we're blending the"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "physical and virtual worlds,"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "we're actually giving the user a"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "very consistent display of the"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "predictions."}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "There's another thing we need to"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "figure out: when does a roll"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "end?"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "Again, games typically don't"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "rely on transient states of a"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "roll; they rely on the result of"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "a roll. When you play a game, you roll"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "some dice, and based on the"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "result of that, your pawn either"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "moves or you make some decision."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "In this case, we may want to"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "animate something or provide"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "feedback to the user."}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "And you may have noticed in the"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "demos that I just showed, I"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "didn't show the numbers until"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "the roll had ended."}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "So how do we do this?"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "Well, first we need to ask our"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "self, what do we observe?"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "In this case, we notice that the"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "dice stop moving and the values"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "are stable between different"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "camera frames."}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "So can machine learning help us"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "here?"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "Perhaps we could build a"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "sequential model that takes in"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "frames and decides when the roll"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "has ended, but we already have a"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "model that has a really good"}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "understanding of dice on the"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "table. So what we really need to do is"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "interpret the output of our"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "model."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "So let's take a look at how to"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "do this in code."}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "Here we have a function that"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "takes in two lists of object"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "observations: one from the"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "current camera frame and one"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "from the previous camera frame."}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "So there's a few things we need"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "to check in order to decide that"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "the roll has ended."}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "The first is, do we have as many"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "dice now as we had before?"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "If not, maybe one die has"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "entered the camera frame, so we"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "now have more than before."}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "If we have less than before,"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "maybe one of them is bouncing"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "around so the detector isn't"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "picking that up."}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "So if we don't have as many now"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "as before, the roll is still"}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "happening. Next we're going to compare each"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "of the observations in the"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "previous prediction and in the"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "current one."}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "If the values represented on top"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "of the dice aren't the same, our"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "roll has not ended yet."}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "And we also check that the"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "bounding boxes overlap between"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "these predictions by more than"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "85%."}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "If the bounding boxes between"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "the prediction we're looking at"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "and the one we're comparing it"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "with don't overlap, either we're"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "looking at two completely"}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "different dice, or it's the same"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "one that has moved by a"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "significant amount."}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "Finally, if we have as many"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "matches now as we have dice on"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "the table, the roll has ended."}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "So now that our app can find,"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "count, recognize dice on a table"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "and figuring out the end of a"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "roll, we have a foundation for"}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "building something more."}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "And it's time to talk about the"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "next steps of our journey."}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "To do that, I'd like to welcome"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "Brent back up to the stage."}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "Thank you, Scott."}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "As Scott said, our app can now"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "recognize dice on the table."}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "The next thing we need to look"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "at is, how do we handle user"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "input? We know that our users are going"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "to be entering numbers into our"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "app, because we're practicing"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "math skills. And we could've just put a large"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "number pad up on the screen and"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "have them tap in the numbers,"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "but we wanted to facilitate a"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "more natural interaction with"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "the app."}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "And remember: we're working with"}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "children here, and children are"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "also practicing writing their"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "numbers."}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "So we thought, why not just let"}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "them draw directly on the"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "screen? Well, to do this, we're going to"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "need our app to be able to"}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "recognize handwritten digits."}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "Fortunately, machine learning is"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "already doing a very good job at"}, {"start": 1036.0, "text": "solving this problem; in fact,"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "there's an entire dataset"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "available to let you train your"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "own models to recognize"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "handwritten digits."}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "It's called MNIST."}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "Well, we did that, and we put"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "that model on our new Core ML"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "Models page."}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "So let's take a look in code at"}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "how we'd use this model."}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "We're going to use Vision and"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "PencilKit here."}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "We set up Vision to use our Core"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "ML model; in this case,"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "MNISTClassifier."}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "Next, we get our image from the"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "PencilKit canvas view."}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "After that, we set up our Vision"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "request handler to use that"}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "Then, we perform the request and"}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "we get the results."}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "It's as easy as that."}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "So we integrated this into our"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "model, and it started working"}, {"start": 1088.0, "text": "pretty well. We were recognizing quite a few"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "handwritten digits."}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "But as we started drawing some"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "larger digits, we noticed"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "something interesting: our model"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "was sometimes getting the"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "predictions incorrect."}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "So what's happening?"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "Well, to understand, we need to"}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "see what image is being input to"}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "our model. And we can do that in Xcode."}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "So we set a break point where we"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "get the image from PencilKit,"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "and we use Xcode's quick view to"}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "actually look at what that image"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "is. And when we did, we saw"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "something interesting: our 7s"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "from the example are not looking"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "like 7s to the model."}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "They're looking a lot more like"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "1s."}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "So what's happening here?"}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "We need to think about what the"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "model's expecting for an input."}, {"start": 1142.0, "text": "This model is expecting a 28 by"}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "28 pixel image, but the image"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "that we get drawn on the screen"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "is much bigger than that."}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "So to get the image in the right"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "format, we have to downscale it."}, {"start": 1156.0, "text": "But as we downscaled it, we lost"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "information about the strokes"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "that were being drawn on the screen, and our 7s started"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "looking a lot more like 1s."}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "Once we knew that, the fix was"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "pretty easy: we just needed to"}, {"start": 1169.0, "text": "have a thicker stroke on the"}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "screen. And when we did that, after we"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "downscaled, our images going to"}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "the model looked a lot more like"}, {"start": 1178.0, "text": "what was being drawn on the"}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "screen, and the model started"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "getting the predictions correct."}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "PencilKit makes this really"}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "easy."}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "Here we have allowsFingerDrawing"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "set to true, since we're drawing"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "on the screen with our fingers;"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "and then, we set the tool to be"}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "something like a marker with a"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "thicker stroke."}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "All right. Our model is now predicting"}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "single digits really well, but"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "we have another couple"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "challenges."}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "Some digits are written with"}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "multiple strokes."}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "Our model takes a static image"}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "of a digit, not stroke"}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "information about that digit."}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "So how do we know when to take"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "what's being drawn on the screen"}, {"start": 1226.0, "text": "and pass it to our model to get"}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "a prediction?"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "Additionally, since we're adding"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "dice or possibly multiplying"}, {"start": 1235.0, "text": "dice, we may be working with"}, {"start": 1236.0, "text": "numbers that have multiple"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "digits, and our model is only"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "trained to recognize single"}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "digits, not multiple digits."}, {"start": 1244.0, "text": "So how do we handle that?"}, {"start": 1246.0, "text": "We could've used machine"}, {"start": 1247.0, "text": "learning to solve these"}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "problems. We could've trained a model to"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "recognize stroke information"}, {"start": 1251.0, "text": "about digits, or we could've"}, {"start": 1254.0, "text": "trained a model to recognize"}, {"start": 1255.0, "text": "numbers with multiple digits,"}, {"start": 1256.0, "text": "but we already know a lot of"}, {"start": 1258.0, "text": "information about what's being"}, {"start": 1260.0, "text": "drawn on the screen."}, {"start": 1261.0, "text": "So instead, we decided to solve"}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "this problem programmatically,"}, {"start": 1264.0, "text": "and I'll show you how."}, {"start": 1266.0, "text": "Let's take this example."}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "Someone draws the first stroke"}, {"start": 1271.0, "text": "of a 1 on the screen."}, {"start": 1272.0, "text": "We take that, we pass it as an"}, {"start": 1275.0, "text": "image to our model, and we get a"}, {"start": 1276.0, "text": "prediction, and it's a 1."}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "Next, they draw the second"}, {"start": 1280.0, "text": "stroke of a 1, the base."}, {"start": 1283.0, "text": "We look to see if any of that"}, {"start": 1285.0, "text": "stroke is overlapping any of the"}, {"start": 1287.0, "text": "first stroke."}, {"start": 1289.0, "text": "Since it is, we know that it's"}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "the same number, so we get rid"}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "of the first prediction, we"}, {"start": 1294.0, "text": "combine the first stroke with"}, {"start": 1295.0, "text": "the second stroke into one"}, {"start": 1297.0, "text": "image, and we pass that entire"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "image to the model."}, {"start": 1300.0, "text": "And that gets predicted to be a"}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "1."}, {"start": 1302.0, "text": "Next, the user draws another"}, {"start": 1305.0, "text": "stroke on the screen."}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "We look at that third stroke and"}, {"start": 1309.0, "text": "see if any of it overlaps either"}, {"start": 1311.0, "text": "of the first two strokes."}, {"start": 1313.0, "text": "Since it doesn't, we know that"}, {"start": 1315.0, "text": "it's a separate number, so we"}, {"start": 1316.0, "text": "pass it separately to the model,"}, {"start": 1318.0, "text": "and it gets predicted to be a 2."}, {"start": 1322.0, "text": "Now I'd like to invite Scott"}, {"start": 1323.0, "text": "back up to show you this in the"}, {"start": 1325.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 1326.0, "text": "Scott?"}, {"start": 1331.0, "text": "Thanks, Brent."}, {"start": 1333.0, "text": "We now have an updated app that"}, {"start": 1335.0, "text": "still has our object detector"}, {"start": 1336.0, "text": "that's able to detect and"}, {"start": 1338.0, "text": "classify dice and their values,"}, {"start": 1341.0, "text": "but we've also added the ability"}, {"start": 1342.0, "text": "to draw input just like Brent"}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "discussed with you."}, {"start": 1345.0, "text": "So I think it's time to do some"}, {"start": 1347.0, "text": "math."}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "Here, the user has the option to"}, {"start": 1351.0, "text": "either add the values displayed"}, {"start": 1353.0, "text": "on the dice or multiply them."}, {"start": 1355.0, "text": "And so to keep things simple,"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "I'm going to start with"}, {"start": 1357.0, "text": "addition."}, {"start": 1358.0, "text": "So let's see how input handling"}, {"start": 1360.0, "text": "works."}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "Yes."}, {"start": 1371.0, "text": "So if we multiply these values,"}, {"start": 1373.0, "text": "I'm pretty sure we get 24."}, {"start": 1376.0, "text": "Now, that's an interesting number."}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "I want you to pay close"}, {"start": 1378.0, "text": "attention to what happens when I"}, {"start": 1380.0, "text": "draw the 4 on screen."}, {"start": 1382.0, "text": "If you think about a 4 that's"}, {"start": 1384.0, "text": "drawn with two strokes, our"}, {"start": 1386.0, "text": "model's going to have a pretty"}, {"start": 1387.0, "text": "hard time figuring out that's a"}, {"start": 1388.0, "text": "4 when it only sees the first"}, {"start": 1390.0, "text": "stroke, so it may predict some"}, {"start": 1391.0, "text": "other digit until I draw the"}, {"start": 1393.0, "text": "second stroke."}, {"start": 1395.0, "text": "Let's have a look."}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "Did you notice that the first"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "stroke of my 4 was predicted as"}, {"start": 1404.0, "text": "a 1, but as soon as I had the"}, {"start": 1405.0, "text": "second stroke, that was a 4?"}, {"start": 1407.0, "text": "There's one other answer that is"}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "always correct, and I just want"}, {"start": 1413.0, "text": "to show you more 4s, so let's"}, {"start": 1414.0, "text": "try it."}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "Cool. So our app can recognize"}, {"start": 1423.0, "text": "dice on the table, understand a"}, {"start": 1425.0, "text": "roll, it can check our math, we"}, {"start": 1427.0, "text": "can input that using drawing to"}, {"start": 1430.0, "text": "draw the digits on screen, but"}, {"start": 1432.0, "text": "we're talking about blending the"}, {"start": 1433.0, "text": "physical and virtual worlds"}, {"start": 1435.0, "text": "together, so we thought it would"}, {"start": 1436.0, "text": "be a lot of fun and also very"}, {"start": 1438.0, "text": "interactive if the kids playing"}, {"start": 1441.0, "text": "with our game could input their"}, {"start": 1442.0, "text": "answers in the form of voice."}, {"start": 1444.0, "text": "So let's take a look at that."}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "Again, I'm going to add or"}, {"start": 1449.0, "text": "multiply these two together and"}, {"start": 1450.0, "text": "get 24."}, {"start": 1451.0, "text": "And let's do that using speech."}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "Twenty-four."}, {"start": 1457.0, "text": "Cool."}, {"start": 1461.0, "text": "This is super easy to do using"}, {"start": 1462.0, "text": "the speech framework."}, {"start": 1463.0, "text": "And new this year in speech, we"}, {"start": 1469.0, "text": "have offline speech recognition."}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "This means that speech"}, {"start": 1474.0, "text": "recognition can work in your app"}, {"start": 1476.0, "text": "even when your device is not"}, {"start": 1477.0, "text": "connected to the internet."}, {"start": 1479.0, "text": "And if you really want your"}, {"start": 1481.0, "text": "user's data to remain on their"}, {"start": 1483.0, "text": "device, you can actually require"}, {"start": 1485.0, "text": "speech recognition to happen on"}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "device by setting"}, {"start": 1488.0, "text": "requiresOnDeviceRecognition to"}, {"start": 1490.0, "text": "true on your speech recognizer."}, {"start": 1494.0, "text": "So now our app can understand a"}, {"start": 1496.0, "text": "dice roll and handle input in"}, {"start": 1498.0, "text": "various different ways, but we"}, {"start": 1500.0, "text": "need to move on with our journey"}, {"start": 1502.0, "text": "and finish this up."}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "So I'd like to welcome Brent"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "back up to the stage."}, {"start": 1511.0, "text": "Thank you, Scott."}, {"start": 1517.0, "text": "As Scott mentioned, we have our"}, {"start": 1521.0, "text": "app recognizing dice, and we"}, {"start": 1524.0, "text": "know how to handle user input."}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "But we said this was going to be"}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "a game, right?"}, {"start": 1530.0, "text": "So let's make it that."}, {"start": 1534.0, "text": "Next we're going to integrate in"}, {"start": 1536.0, "text": "ARKit and really finalize the"}, {"start": 1538.0, "text": "whole experience."}, {"start": 1539.0, "text": "Of course, any game needs rules,"}, {"start": 1545.0, "text": "so let's go over those first."}, {"start": 1550.0, "text": "Our game is played on a circular"}, {"start": 1552.0, "text": "board with nine sections."}, {"start": 1555.0, "text": "Each player starts on section"}, {"start": 1558.0, "text": "one, and the goal is to move"}, {"start": 1560.0, "text": "clockwise around the board and"}, {"start": 1562.0, "text": "land directly on section nine."}, {"start": 1565.0, "text": "A roll that's too small, and you"}, {"start": 1569.0, "text": "don't go far enough."}, {"start": 1572.0, "text": "A roll that's too large, and"}, {"start": 1574.0, "text": "you're going to overshoot your"}, {"start": 1578.0, "text": "goal. During each player's turn, they"}, {"start": 1580.0, "text": "roll the dice, and they have two"}, {"start": 1582.0, "text": "options: they can take the sum"}, {"start": 1585.0, "text": "of that dice and move that"}, {"start": 1587.0, "text": "number in a clockwise direction,"}, {"start": 1589.0, "text": "or they can take the difference"}, {"start": 1590.0, "text": "of the dice and move that number"}, {"start": 1593.0, "text": "in a clockwise direction."}, {"start": 1595.0, "text": "So Scott, you up for a game?"}, {"start": 1610.0, "text": "So we've now integrated our"}, {"start": 1611.0, "text": "virtual board into our ARKit"}, {"start": 1613.0, "text": "game that's also using Core ML"}, {"start": 1616.0, "text": "to recognize dice."}, {"start": 1618.0, "text": "How about you start off, Brent?"}, {"start": 1619.0, "text": "Sounds good."}, {"start": 1621.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 1622.0, "text": "The 5 -- I've got a 5 and a 2."}, {"start": 1626.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 1627.0, "text": "I think I'm going to add those."}, {"start": 1635.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 1636.0, "text": "Ooh, you got really close."}, {"start": 1637.0, "text": "Close."}, {"start": 1642.0, "text": "So we got 6 and 1; I can"}, {"start": 1644.0, "text": "either subtract these and get 5"}, {"start": 1647.0, "text": "or add them and join Brent on"}, {"start": 1649.0, "text": "the 8 slot, so let's add these."}, {"start": 1657.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 1658.0, "text": "I don't think I'm going to be"}, {"start": 1661.0, "text": "able to get a 1."}, {"start": 1662.0, "text": "Let's see."}, {"start": 1667.0, "text": "I think I'll subtract this time."}, {"start": 1669.0, "text": "Let me do a 2."}, {"start": 1679.0, "text": "Okay. So I got 6 and 1 again."}, {"start": 1681.0, "text": "This time I'm going to change it"}, {"start": 1682.0, "text": "up and do a 5."}, {"start": 1685.0, "text": "And Brent really thinks -- yeah."}, {"start": 1688.0, "text": "Brent thinks I draw funny 5s."}, {"start": 1690.0, "text": "You know, this game could"}, {"start": 1693.0, "text": "probably go on pretty long, but"}, {"start": 1696.0, "text": "I think Scott might've mentioned"}, {"start": 1698.0, "text": "something about a number always"}, {"start": 1700.0, "text": "being correct, so let's see if"}, {"start": 1703.0, "text": "this works in our game."}, {"start": 1708.0, "text": "Ah, you found the secret,"}, {"start": 1709.0, "text": "Brent."}, {"start": 1710.0, "text": "Good job."}, {"start": 1711.0, "text": "Success."}, {"start": 1723.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 1724.0, "text": "Today we looked at combining"}, {"start": 1727.0, "text": "multiple technologies together"}, {"start": 1729.0, "text": "to blend our physical and"}, {"start": 1731.0, "text": "virtual worlds."}, {"start": 1733.0, "text": "We built an experience that goes"}, {"start": 1734.0, "text": "beyond any single technology and"}, {"start": 1737.0, "text": "it let us play this fun game in"}, {"start": 1738.0, "text": "this enhanced new world."}, {"start": 1741.0, "text": "We used object detection to"}, {"start": 1743.0, "text": "recognize dice on the table."}, {"start": 1747.0, "text": "We used image classification to"}, {"start": 1749.0, "text": "recognize handwritten digits on"}, {"start": 1751.0, "text": "the screen."}, {"start": 1752.0, "text": "We used speech recognition as"}, {"start": 1754.0, "text": "another way to interact with our"}, {"start": 1755.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 1756.0, "text": "And we brought in ARKit to"}, {"start": 1758.0, "text": "really finalize the whole"}, {"start": 1759.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 1762.0, "text": "If you'd like more information,"}, {"start": 1764.0, "text": "please see our session 228 on"}, {"start": 1766.0, "text": "the developer website or come"}, {"start": 1768.0, "text": "talk to us in the labs tomorrow."}, {"start": 1770.0, "text": "Thank you, and have a great rest"}]}